Sprite sheets are the source; the exhibit page actually plays them now

Two things to say first, because they change what you were expecting.

**The exhibit page has never played anything.** I went looking for the frame
player you hoped predated the mp4s and there isn't one — the nine .qr-slot
entries were static text reading "emitter pending, the loop will play here", and
no JavaScript anywhere touched them. Only the static bootstrap QR in the header
was ever real. So this isn't a rewiring, it's the first time.

**The mp4s were never a good source and neither were the 552px frames.** A QR
frame is 69 modules across. The rendered PNGs bake 8 pixels per module, which is
64x more pixels than the code carries. So the canonical form here is one pixel
per module, every frame packed into a single sheet: the whole EliseAI loop is a
552x552 PNG at 54KB, smaller than its own mp4, with no frame rate baked in.
3.7MB for all ten, against 4.3MB of mp4.

Proven, not assumed: verify-sprite.mjs slices a sheet the way a player would,
reads every cell with anecdote.channel's own decoder, and reassembles through
carrierSession. 100% of cells decode, payloads come back byte-exact with valid
signatures, and the cell counts land on the predicted 1.2*K. The sheet needs no
other artifact.

mp4s moved to _intermediates/ with _format-probe/, and the README says plainly
why they are not library material.

**Every slot names its own source in the markup**, which is what you asked for:

    <li class="qr-slot" id="slot-cite-autumn-ryan-verra-mobility"
        data-sprite="library/lucky-sevens/verra-mobility.png"
        data-frames="148" data-cols="13" data-cell="69" data-fps="15">

No manifest fetch, no indirection — read the HTML and you know what is on screen.
Change data-fps and it changes speed. Scaling is nearest-neighbour everywhere
(image-rendering: pixelated, imageSmoothingEnabled false), because a smoothly
resampled QR stops reading.

The emitter also measures itself: below 3.2 device px per module — 221px at 69
modules, the floor measured against the real decoder — it adds .too-small-to-scan
and shows a red outline rather than quietly serving a code no camera can read.
That guard caught a real bug while I built this: the canvas had landed in the
2rem marker column of the slot grid and was rendering at 40px. Fixed, and the
guard is why I noticed.

Also updated COLLECTORATE.videoId to nw_kLlOEvA4 for the unlisted demo.

Two things I noticed and did not touch:
- notes/lucky-sevens/links.json has 29 spans of cosmetic link text, and nothing
  on the page consumes it yet. Happy to wire it to the lyric pager next if that
  is where it is meant to go.
- The live site was serving a stale Cloudflare Pages build as of last week. If
  these don't appear after merge, that is why, and it needs the Pages dashboard
  rather than anything in this repo.
